  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">FemFocus &#x2013; Encouraging Women Entrepreneurship &#x2013; AFRICA - Stichting Women Win - Kenya, Uganda, South Africa, Nigeria</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This programme, part of the FemFocus subsidy grant framework, aims to contribute to the policy goals as stated in the framework:

1. strengthen women&#x2019;s entrepreneurship at the individual level; and
2. remove socio-cultural and institutional barriers at the societal level.

The programme will be implemented in Uganda, South Africa, Kenya and Nigeria.

The programme focuses on strengthening these local intermediary organisations so they can coordinate services and tackle structural barriers at scale. It targets three interconnected challenges:
1. Insufficient organisational capacity of local support organisations.
2. Limited access to capital and markets, and persistent structural barriers for women entrepreneurs.
3. Weak ecosystem coordination among public, private and civil-society actors.

To address these, the programme uses three main types of interventions: grants, capacity strengthening, and network brokering

The programme will facilitate coordination and knowledge exchange between ecosystem actors to reduce fragmentation and close coordination gaps. By brokering networks and partnerships, it aims to create a more coherent, gender-responsive support system and to mitigate structural barriers.

Concrete activities within these three intervention areas will be designed together with in-country partners during the inception phase, ensuring that the programme is adapted to local contexts and needs.</narrative>
  </description>
